# Exact optional property types

`tsconfig.json` has `"exactOptionalPropertyTypes": true`.

For `prop?: T`, TypeScript allows **omitting** the key or assigning `T`. It does **not** allow `prop: undefined` unless the type includes `undefined` (`prop?: T | undefined`).

Docs: [Exact Optional Property Types](https://www.typescriptlang.org/tsconfig/#exactOptionalPropertyTypes)

```ts
type Theme = {
	colorThemeOverride?: "dark" | "light"
}

const ok: Theme = { colorThemeOverride: "dark" }
const alsoOk: Theme = {}
// ❌ const bad: Theme = { colorThemeOverride: undefined }

type ThemeExplicit = {
	colorThemeOverride?: "dark" | "light" | undefined
}
const withUndefined: ThemeExplicit = { colorThemeOverride: undefined } // ✅
```

When spreading or assigning partials, omit the key (`delete` / conditional spread) instead of setting `undefined`, unless `| undefined` is intentional in the type.
